./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0034/committee2/theory_skeptic.out:21:RATIONALE: The L0 follow-up is methodologically honest and the pre-registered ELSE branch fired correctly, but the underlying modeling exercise cannot, even in principle, settle the empirical claim: every positive result is a mechanical consequence of the simulator (online > static, lead-time > 0 by construction), and every negative result is a free-parameter choice (sigma_conf). The prior-art kill (Mavi 2511.07364 at AUC ~0.9 on online stepwise failure detection; Vasudev 2602.03338 at AUROC 0.94) is the load-bearing finding — and it does not depend on the sim at all. Under the claim's own framing (must beat self-confidence AND difficulty with measured lead time), the published online stepwise self-evaluators occupy exactly that niche at calibration levels (~0.9) where this L0's own model predicts the monitor LOSES. The 42% lead-time coverage already failed the pre-registered bar in EXP-0033. The "distinct from difficulty" residual win is the information-set-asymmetry tautology, not a substantive contribution. RED: relabeling of online stepwise failure detection with an unsupported lead-time framing; do not spend GPU L1.
